# Drafted by Gemini (R26 Dusk Mother), edited. The Dusk Mother: hook, clues, weakness, the lair fight and the aftermath.

~ arrive
set mf_dusk_arrived
Narrator: A homestead at the edge of a spider forest, cots empty, shutters hung with white thread, a doll on every windowsill.
check Dexterity DC 20 -> arrive_ok | arrive_hit

~ arrive_ok
Narrator: You cut a path through the webs with a blade and the poison never touches you.
set mf_dusk_resisted
-> END

~ arrive_hit
Narrator: Webs catch a hero and the spiders' poison burns in their veins before they cut free.
damage 4d10 poison party
-> END

~ region
Narrator: You walk the Webwoods, and strands of web drape across the path like ribbons.
time +60
check Dexterity DC 20 -> arrive_ok | arrive_hit

~ hook
mf_ysolde_teen [angry]: She says her brothers and sisters were taken from their beds, and the grown folk walk about like sacks and will not say why.
set mf_dusk_asked
quest mf_dusk asked
-> menu

~ hook_again
mf_ysolde_teen [sad]: She says another cot was empty this morning, and asks if you have found them.
-> menu

~ menu
* Ask what has been happening -> trouble
* Ask where it comes from -> where
* [if not flag.mf_dusk_found] Ask how to find it -> route_a
* Say we will deal with it -> END

~ trouble
mf_ysolde_teen [afraid]: Webs choke the woods, wails come at every hour, and the grown ones are empty as dolls, stitched at the seams.
-> menu

~ where
mf_ysolde_teen [sad]: She says a seamstress went mad and killed her children while possessed, and now she weeps in white, taking the rest.
-> menu

~ route_a
mf_ysolde_teen [neutral]: She says the children's rhymes hold what happened, if someone puts the verses together.
* [Arcana DC 20] Piece together the children's rhymes -> a_ok | a_slow
* [History DC 20] Match the verses to what the old folk remember -> a_ok | a_slow
* Gather every rhyme the children ever sang, however long it takes -> a_slow
* Another time -> menu

~ a_ok
mf_ysolde_teen [smile]: The rhymes fit together into a story, and the last verse names the hut where the seamstress still sits.
time +60
set mf_dusk_found
set mf_dusk_clue_a
quest mf_dusk trail
-> menu

~ a_slow
Narrator: It takes all night to gather the rhymes, but laid together they point to the hut in the woods.
time +300
set mf_dusk_found
quest mf_dusk trail
-> menu

~ clue
mf_pennywhistle_nurse [smile]: She says she has been waiting for someone sensible, and sets her mending aside to look you over.
set mf_dusk_clue_met
-> clue_menu

~ clue_again
mf_pennywhistle_nurse [neutral]: A short greeting back, in character, that welcomes the heroes to ask again.
-> clue_menu

~ clue_menu
* Ask about it -> clue_talk
* [if not flag.mf_dusk_found] Ask how to find it -> route_b
* [if flag.mf_dusk_found and not flag.mf_dusk_weak] Ask what could hurt it -> weak
* Take our leave -> END

~ clue_talk
mf_pennywhistle_nurse [sad]: She says the seamstress's own children were small and loved their toys, and that their toys are what the weeping thing cannot bear to see.
-> clue_menu

~ route_b
mf_pennywhistle_nurse [neutral]: She says the spiders of the Webwoods go straight to the hut as to a hearth; follow them and you will not go wrong.
* [Animal Handling DC 20] Follow the spiders through the Webwoods -> b_ok | b_slow
* [Survival DC 20] Read the webs for the way to the hut -> b_ok | b_slow
* Follow the webs the long way round -> b_slow
* Another time -> clue_menu

~ b_ok
mf_pennywhistle_nurse [smile]: The spiders lead you unerringly, a river of small legs, to the hut in the clearing.
time +60
set mf_dusk_found
set mf_dusk_clue_b
quest mf_dusk trail
-> clue_menu

~ b_slow
Narrator: You lose hours to wrong turns in the webs, but the spiders do at last bring you to the clearing.
time +300
set mf_dusk_found
quest mf_dusk trail
-> clue_menu

~ weak
mf_pennywhistle_nurse [sad]: She presses a small bundle on you: the children's toys, saved from the fire. Show them to the Mother and she will not be able to fight.
* [Insight DC 20] Read the toys for the children's memories -> weak_ok | weak_slow
* [Investigation DC 20] Gather the toys and the children's spirits gently -> weak_ok | weak_slow
* Hold each toy and wait, slowly, for it to speak -> weak_slow
* Another time -> clue_menu

~ weak_ok
mf_pennywhistle_nurse [sad]: The toys hold the shape of small hands, and when you turn them over each one seems to hum a lullaby.
time +60
give mf_children_toys
set mf_dusk_weak
quest mf_dusk ready
-> clue_menu

~ weak_slow
Narrator: You sit with the toys through a long hour, quietly, until each is ready to be shown.
time +300
give mf_children_toys
set mf_dusk_weak
quest mf_dusk ready
-> clue_menu

~ lair
Narrator: The seamstress's hut stands in the clearing, small from outside, its door ajar and a sound of shears inside.
* Go in and face it -> fight
* Not yet -> END

~ fight
cutscene mf_dusk_reveals
Narrator: The Dusk Mother rises from her loom, a weeping shade in white, huge shears in her hands, a doll hanging from each finger.
cutscene mf_dusk_reveals_2
Narrator: She wails, and the whole hut seems to listen.
cutscene end
if flag.mf_dusk_weak
combat mf_dusk_weak
elif level >= 19
combat mf_dusk_full
else
combat mf_dusk_light
endif

~ aftermath
cutscene mf_dusk_falls
Narrator: The Dusk Mother's shears fall, her shape dissolves into dust and white thread, and from the hut small voices laugh, once.
cutscene mf_dusk_falls_2
Narrator: The moon turns its face slowly north and east, toward the burning hill.
cutscene end
set mf_dusk_aftermath
set old_fears_slain += 1
set moonfall_credit += 1
set moonfall_nights_left += 1
give bell_of_the_dusk_mother
quest mf_dusk slain
xp milestone
Narrator: Beyond the moors Rowan's Rise cracks open, and a red light shines.
-> END
